SAMPLE DISTRICT AI NEEDS ASSESSMENT:

District: [District Name] | Population: ~4,200 students | Date: [Date]
Prepared by: [Name/Role] | AI Tools Used: [Specify] | Status: DRAFT – PENDING REVIEW

EXECUTIVE SUMMARY:
This needs assessment examines our district's readiness for responsible AI integration across instructional, operational, and leadership domains.

SECTION 1: CURRENT STATE ANALYSIS

1a. Technology Infrastructure
- 1:1 device program: Grades 4-12 ✓ | Grades K-3: Shared carts
- Broadband: 85% of classrooms have adequate bandwidth; 3 buildings need upgrade
- AI tool access: Limited (no district-wide agreements); teachers using consumer tools ad hoc
- Data privacy: No current AI-specific data governance policy

1b. Staff Capacity Survey Results (n=187 staff, 73% response rate)
- "I understand what AI is": 68% agree or strongly agree
- "I feel prepared to use AI responsibly": 31% agree or strongly agree
- "I have received training on AI in education": 12% agree or strongly agree
- "I am concerned about student AI misuse": 84% agree or strongly agree

1c. Student AI Awareness (n=450, grades 6-12)
- 78% have used AI tools outside of school
- 34% have used AI to complete school assignments
- 22% have received formal instruction on AI ethics/use

SECTION 2: PRIORITY NEEDS IDENTIFIED

Priority 1 – URGENT: Data Privacy & Governance Policy
No AI-specific policy exists. Staff using unapproved consumer tools with potential student data exposure.
Recommendation: Adopt AI Acceptable Use Policy before any formal rollout. Target: Q1.

Priority 2 – HIGH: Staff Professional Learning
Only 12% of staff have received AI training.
Recommendation: Enroll all instructional staff in VCSU AI Institute program. Target: Year 1.

Priority 3 – MEDIUM: Infrastructure Upgrade
3 buildings need bandwidth improvements to support AI tools at scale.
Recommendation: Budget request for network upgrades. Target: Year 2.

Priority 4 – MEDIUM: Student Digital Literacy Curriculum
Students using AI without guidance creates academic integrity and safety risks.
Recommendation: Embed AI literacy into K-12 curriculum scope and sequence. Target: Year 1-2.

SECTION 3: RECOMMENDED ACTION PLAN

Phase 1 (Months 1-3): Policy + Leadership Preparation
Phase 2 (Months 4-9): Staff Professional Learning (VCSU AI Institute)
Phase 3 (Months 10-18): Classroom Integration + Student Curriculum
Phase 4 (Year 2+): Evaluation, Iteration, Advanced Implementation

APPENDIX: Full survey data, focus group notes, and benchmark comparisons available upon request.

